@metadata
title = Text and formatting
summary = Headings, paragraphs, quotes, lists, checklists and inline marks.
@endmetadata

# Text and formatting

The prose layer is deliberately small. Everything structural is a directive.

## Headings

@code(language="text")
# Title
## Section
### Subsection
@endcode

One to six `#` characters followed by a space. A renderer gives each heading an
anchor derived from its text, so sections can be linked directly — the contents
list on this page is built from them.

## Paragraphs

Consecutive lines separated by a blank line. A single newline inside a
paragraph is a soft wrap, not a break, so you can wrap your source at whatever
column you like without changing the output.

@code(language="text")
This sentence and the one after it
are the same paragraph.

This is a new one.
@endcode

## Quotes

@code(language="text")
> Something worth quoting.
@endcode

## Lists

@code(language="text")
- one
- two
* also a bullet

1. first
2. second
@endcode

@note
Title: Lists do not nest
Indenting an item deeper than the first does not create a sublist. XTXT reports
a warning there rather than flattening it silently, so a formatting mistake
cannot quietly destroy your structure. This is the format's biggest limitation
and is covered on the Limitations page.
@endnote

## Checklists

An unordered item whose text begins with `[ ]` or `[x]`:

@code(language="text")
- [ ] not done yet
- [x] done
@endcode

These are picked up by `xtxt extract` as tasks alongside `@task` blocks, so a
casual checklist and a formal record both reach a program.

## Inline marks

@table
Write | Get
------|----
`*emphasis*` | *emphasis*
`**strong**` | **strong**
`` `code` `` | `code`
`~~strike~~` | ~~strike~~
`[text](url)` | a link
@endtable

## Escaping

A backslash makes the next character literal:

@code(language="text")
\*not emphasis\*
@endcode

## Footnotes

@code(language="text")
Parsing is a single pass[^why].

@footnote(id="why")
Nothing nests, so no backtracking is needed.
@endfootnote
@endcode

A reference to an id with no footnote, and a footnote nothing references, are
both warnings.
